---
title: HCML Monitoring Portal — Server flow (one request through the BFF)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    %% =================================================================
    %%  SERVER FLOW -- one GET /api/sites, end to end, in the order the
    %%  BFF actually runs it. Read top to bottom: that order is the
    %%  design. A Fastify hook only covers the routes registered after
    %%  it, so index.ts registers helmet, CORS, the rate limit, the
    %%  compression hook, the error handler and the auth guard BEFORE
    %%  any route module.

    %%  The Zabbix token exists only inside portal-bff. It is never sent
    %%  to the browser and never appears in a log line.

    %%  The two 503s in the red band are DELIBERATE, not a typo for 502
    %%  or 504: a rejected token and an unreachable Zabbix are
    %%  CONFIGURATION states, not upstream faults, and errors.ts returns
    %%  503 for both (pinned by routes.test.ts and zabbix.test.ts).
    %%  Only zabbix_error is a 502. Nothing in the server ever returns
    %%  504. Do not "correct" these back.

    %%  A miss on /api/sites issues FOUR methods across three cache keys
    %%  with three different TTLs -- host.get (hosts:meta, 30 s),
    %%  problem.get (problems, 5 s) plus trigger.get because problem.get
    %%  carries no host names, and item.get (icmp:hosts, 15 s) for the
    %%  ICMP readings. hostgroup.get is NOT called here: host groups
    %%  ride along as selectHostGroups on host.get. hostgroup.get
    %%  belongs to /api/hosts and /api/reports.
    %% =================================================================

    participant B as Browser
    participant N as nginx<br/>portal-web
    participant F as Fastify<br/>portal-bff
    participant C as TTL cache<br/>in memory
    participant Z as Zabbix API<br/>JSON-RPC 2.0

    B->>N: GET /bff/api/sites<br/>Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
    N->>F: GET /api/sites<br/>X-Forwarded-For preserved

    rect rgb(241, 245, 249)
        Note over F: The plugin chain, in registration order
        F->>F: helmet — security headers<br/>CSP off: this process serves JSON only
        F->>F: CORS — one allowed origin (WEB_ORIGIN)
        F->>F: rate limit — per IP, before auth,<br/>so a flood is rejected before JWT work
        F->>F: compression hook — brotli / gzip
    end

    alt rate limit exceeded
        F-->>B: 429 rate_limited<br/>"the limit is N per minute"
    end

    rect rgb(254, 243, 199)
        Note over F: onRequest auth guard
        F->>F: verify the JWT — header, or ?token= for SSE
        F->>F: requiredRole(url) — first match wins,<br/>anything unmatched needs viewer
    end

    alt no or bad token
        F-->>B: 401 unauthorized — "Sign in to continue."
    else role too low
        F-->>B: 403 forbidden — names the role needed
    end

    F->>C: cached("sites", 15 s, fn)

    alt fresh — within TTL
        C-->>F: the stored value
        Note right of C: no Zabbix call at all
    else another request is already fetching
        C-->>F: await the same promise
        Note right of C: coalesced — twenty NOC screens<br/>cost one upstream read
    else stale but inside staleMs
        C-->>F: the old value, now
        C->>Z: one background refresh
        Note right of C: a failed refresh keeps the old value<br/>and is logged, not thrown
    else miss
        C->>Z: host.get · problem.get · trigger.get · item.get
        Z-->>C: raw JSON-RPC result
        C->>C: store, LRU, max 500 keys
    end

    rect rgb(220, 252, 231)
        Note over F: The part Zabbix cannot do
        F->>F: resolveSite() — tag, then host name,<br/>then inventory, then group
        F->>F: roll hosts up per site, worst severity wins
    end

    F-->>N: 200 application/json<br/>content-encoding: br
    N-->>B: same, unbuffered

    rect rgb(254, 226, 226)
        Note over F,Z: When Zabbix does not cooperate
        Z--xF: token rejected → 503 zabbix_auth<br/>"fix the token", not an opaque 500
        Z--xF: no answer in ZABBIX_TIMEOUT_MS → 503 zabbix_timeout
        Z--xF: JSON-RPC error → 502 zabbix_error, carrying Zabbix's own words
        Note over F: the address in ZBX_URL goes to the log,<br/>never into the response body
    end

    rect rgb(237, 233, 254)
        Note over B,Z: The one write, for comparison
        B->>F: POST /api/problems/acknowledge — operator only
        F->>Z: event.acknowledge, on the SEPARATE write token
        F->>C: invalidate("problems", holdMs)
        F->>B: push the new list to every open screen at once
    end
